From 096c9a10343ca69be52f0ebabf15f423f13b17eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: swouapiy <swouapiy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:53:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] leds: pwm: honour retain-state-suspended

leds-pwm always set LED_CORE_SUSPENDRESUME, so the LED core switched every
PWM LED off when the system suspended, whatever the device tree said. Read
retain-state-suspended as leds-gpio does: with it the LED keeps its state
across suspend (BananaOS: the RG DS's power LED shows the handheld asleep,
not off).
---
 drivers/leds/leds-pwm.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/leds/leds-pwm.c b/drivers/leds/leds-pwm.c
index 6c1f2f5..712335e 100644
--- a/drivers/leds/leds-pwm.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/leds-pwm.c
@@ -92,7 +92,12 @@ static int led_pwm_add(struct device *dev, struct led_pwm_priv *priv,
 	led_data->cdev.name = led->name;
 	led_data->cdev.brightness = LED_OFF;
 	led_data->cdev.max_brightness = led->max_brightness;
-	led_data->cdev.flags = LED_CORE_SUSPENDRESUME;
+	/*
+	 * retain-state-suspended: the LED is left as it is while the system
+	 * sleeps (as leds-gpio does), instead of the LED core switching it off
+	 */
+	if (!fwnode_property_read_bool(fwnode, "retain-state-suspended"))
+		led_data->cdev.flags = LED_CORE_SUSPENDRESUME;
 
 	led_data->pwm = devm_fwnode_pwm_get(dev, fwnode, NULL);
 	if (IS_ERR(led_data->pwm))
